# Copy to <tenant>-devops/docker/<component>/Dockerfile.dockerignore.
#
# BuildKit reads an ignore file named after the Dockerfile and sitting beside
# it, which is what lets each component under erun's shared repo-root build
# context carry its own minimal context instead of one root file trying to
# serve every component at once.
#
# Two things are at stake: how much the daemon has to ship on every build, and
# how stable the cache keys are. A file that is in the context but unused still
# perturbs the cache when it changes, so churny directories belong here even
# when they are small.

# Version control and hooks — large, and changes on every commit.
**/.git
**/.githooks
**/.github

# IDE, editor, and agent state.
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/.claude

# Dependency trees: reinstalled inside the image, never copied into it.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/vendor/bundle

# Build outputs and caches — rebuilt in the image, and churn constantly.
**/dist
**/build
**/target
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.gradle
**/.pytest_cache

# Logs, local env, and OS noise.
**/*.log
**/.env.local
**/.DS_Store

# On a large monorepo, prefer the stronger inverse form over this denylist:
# exclude everything, then re-include only what this image builds from, so a
# new sibling directory cannot silently enlarge the context.
#
#   **
#   !__SOURCE_DIR__/**
